                                  dir: `auto`,
                                  style: { "--framer-text-alignment": `justify` },
                                  children: `This intended behaviour then makes the players carefully consider when to block the virus, and when to safely push it away to block another area. However, the first-time user experience during playtests has shown that players sometimes struggle to understand how the virus growth stages work. I did the tutorial for this game with as less verbal  explanation as possible, since I want the players to figure it out themselves by looking at clues in the level design itself. The clues are shown by the placements of the virus, boxes, and the overall layout of the level. Everything goes smoothly during the playtest until the virus growth stage spreading behaviour introduction. My idea to circumvent this is by adding small dialogues that might help them a little. Although there might be a more optimal way to do it without, I believe clarity is the utmost priority in this case.`,
